and `write_log` (logs.rs:34-53) does `std::fs::create_dir_all(&self.inner.logs_dir)`, `OpenOptions::new().create(true).append(true).open(path)`, then `writeln!(file, "{line}")` into an 8 KiB `BufWriter` that flushes to disk whenever it fills. The caller is the per-line streaming callback: `JobCtx::spawn_child` (jobs/job.rs:98-107) passes `Arc::new(move |line| { if let Err(error) = context.progress(line) … })` to `shell.run_streaming`, and `JobCtx::progress` (job.rs:86-88) is `self.manager.record_progress(...)`.

